      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Privacy</p>
        <h2 id="privacy-title" class="section-title mt-5 font-display" data-reveal>Your browsing stays yours.</h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-secondary" data-reveal>
          Magnetite is built EU-first, with the GDPR in mind. There is no Magnetite server your browser reports to.
        </p>
        <dl class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-3 gap-3 sm:gap-4" data-reveal>
          <div class="stat"><dt>telemetry</dt><dd class="font-display text-brass">0</dd></div>
          <div class="stat"><dt>accounts needed</dt><dd class="font-display text-brass">0</dd></div>
          <div class="stat"><dt>words to join a device</dt><dd class="font-display text-brass">24</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <ul class="mt-10 space-y-3.5 text-secondary">
          {
            privacyPoints.map((p, i) => (
              <li class:list={["flex gap-3", `d-${i}`]} data-reveal>
                <span class="tick">
                  <Icon name="check" size={13} />
                </span>
                <span>{p}</span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-9" data-reveal><a href="/privacy/" class="link">Read the privacy policy</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:pt-24" data-reveal>
        <div class="glass rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold">Sync, if you want it</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-secondary">
            Use Magnetite’s free sync server in Germany, or run
            <code class="rounded bg-surface-2 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.875em] text-fg">magnetite-sync</code>, one small
            program and a Postgres database, on your own server. Devices join with a 24-word sync code. No email, no
            password.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-8"><SyncDiagram /></div>
          <p class="mt-6 text-sm"><a href={docs.syncServer} class="link">How to run your own sync server</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Open source -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 pt-16 sm:pt-24" aria-labelledby="oss-title">
    <div class="grid items-center gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.1fr] lg:gap-20">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Open source</p>
        <h2 id="oss-title" class="section-title mt-5 font-display" data-reveal>Every line in the open.</h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-secondary" data-reveal>
          All of Magnetite’s code is public: read it, build it yourself, change it. There is no account to lock features
          behind, and if we ever stop, anyone can carry it on. The EUPL-1.2 copyleft keeps it that way: whoever ships a
          changed version, or runs a changed sync server for others, publishes the changes too.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-3" data-reveal>
          <a href={repo.url} class="btn btn-secondary" data-magnetic="0.2"><Icon name="code" size={18} />Source code</a>
          <a href={docs.contributing} class="btn btn-secondary" data-magnetic="0.2">Contributing</a>
